This is a classic environment-specific issue, and you are completely right to suspect the security layer!
### Why this is happening (and why only in SD)
In your local environment, your API calls are sent as plain JSON. However, in your SD environment, your useApi hook has a global security feature enabled that automatically **encrypts** POST request payloads.
Because of this, the frontend takes your JSON object and turns it into an encrypted string (that's the 'V9W13sPAtmzXhIR2...==' you see in the error).
When this encrypted string hits your backend, your VoucherActionController is strictly looking for a plain JSON @RequestBody ProcessVoucherRequestDto. It has no idea how to convert an encrypted string into a Java object, so it crashes with the JSON_PARSE_ERROR.
### The Fix: Bypassing Encryption
As you requested, we will disable the payload encryption for these specific calls so your SD testing can proceed smoothly. We will add them back later once the backend decryption filter is ready.
Looking at your download-batch API call, your callApi function accepts a 7th parameter (false) to bypass encryption. We need to apply this to all your POST requests.
Here are the exact replacements you need to make in your frontend files.
### 1. Update VoucherAuthorization.jsx
Find the handleSubmitAction function (around line 496) and update the callApi request.
**Replace this:**
```javascript
    try {
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/voucher/workflow/action",
        {
          batchId: viewingBatchId,
          status: statusToSubmit,
          remarks: executorRemarks.trim(),
          overrideScheduleLapse: overrideLapse,
          newScheduledTime: formattedNewSchedule,
        },
        "POST"
      );

```
**With this:**
```javascript
    try {
      const response = await callApi(
        "/JS/voucher/workflow/action",
        {
          batchId: viewingBatchId,
          status: statusToSubmit,
          remarks: executorRemarks.trim(),
          overrideScheduleLapse: overrideLapse,
          newScheduledTime: formattedNewSchedule,
        },
        "POST",
        "json", // responseType
        null,   // customHeaders
        {},     // customConfig
        false   // <--- BYPASSES SD ENCRYPTION
      );

```
